# CODEOWNERS — OpenBurnBar
#
# GitHub requires a review from EVERY owner listed for a touched path before a
# PR is mergeable when "Require review from Code Owners" branch protection is
# on. Listing two owners on the sensitive surfaces below creates real
# separation of duties: the default owner can no longer self-approve a change
# to a release/deploy workflow, the Firestore rules, or a release-critical
# path — the @Ajnunezg/security-reviewers team must also approve.
#
# Separation-of-duties policy (who may sit on the security-reviewers team and
# the solo-operator fallback when no second human exists) is documented in
# docs/SOLO_OPERATOR_POLICY.md. The team handle is required here so the control
# is enforced by GitHub at review time, not by convention.

# Default owner for everything
